analytic bound (construction A, all N >= 20):
  L = log N, t = pi/L.  Since log is increasing:
    n=1                  -> cos = 1
    2 <= n <= sqrt(N)     -> 0 < t log n <= pi/2   -> 0 < cos <= 1
    sqrt(N) < n          -> pi/2 < t log n <= pi   -> cos <= 0
    N/e <= n <= N         -> t log n in [pi-pi/L, pi] -> cos <= -cos(pi/L)
    the interval [N/e,N] contains >= N(1-1/e) integers (right end is N itself)
  hence  Re S_N(pi/log N) <= sqrt(N) - N(1-1/e)cos(pi/L)
                          <= sqrt(N) - N(1-1/e)(1 - pi^2/(2L^2)) = sqrt(N)(1-h(N))
  1 - 1/e  > 0.632352941176 ;  1 - pi^2/(2 log^2 20) > 0.450125280589 ;  sqrt(20) > 4.4721
  h(20) > 1.27292980139  > 1  =>  Re S_N(pi/log N) < 0 for every N >= 20
  h(N) is increasing for N >= 20 (h'/h = 1/(2N) + pi^2/(L^3 N (1-pi^2/(2L^2))) > 0).
  analytic bound status: CERTIFIED (elementary)

